  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I would use the premade mix for bananas sold in the Asian markets next time, too much trouble for nothing better than a cheaper premade mix."
    },
    {
      "text": "A fabulous recipe!! Even better fried with sesame seeds, and drizzled with honey when finished. Ice cream goes perfectly as well."
    },
    {
      "text": "I halved the recipe and followed to the T. The batter came out very thin. I added a tbsp more of both flour and still looked thin. For some reasone after I let it sat for an hour on the counter...it came out thicker, and coated the bananas well. I sprinkle extra coconut on top and drizzled it with condensed milk. It's delicious! Then I tried it with the melted chocolate with a scoop of vanilla ice cream... it's like eating frozen banana but BETTER!"
    },
    {
      "text": "It doesn't get any better than this when they serve them warm drizzled with a sweet Thai honey sauce and served with a Thai vanilla bean coconut ice cream SO GOOD!!!!!"
    }
  ],
